    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Lof3BCv5rxW9qPdtyr7VJs)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no hard dependency.\n- **#437 (crossref resolver in every command)**: both change the \"Chapters in a parent's PDF\" part of `sp-devonthink.org` / `.el` and `tests/sp-devonthink-test.el`. #437 leaves the offset options and page parsing alone; this PR removes them and rewrites `sp-devonthink-resolve`'s page logic. Expect a textual conflict in `sp-devonthink-resolve` and the tests whichever merges second. Resolution: keep #437's `sp-devonthink-record`, and keep this PR's label lookup in place of the offset arithmetic. The offset steps in #437's Manual testing (`sp-devonthink-parent-page-offsets`) no longer apply after this PR.\n- **#436** (merged): this PR removes `sp-devonthink-page-offset`, `sp-devonthink-parent-page-offsets` and `sp-devonthink-first-page` that #436 added.\n- **#419 (ADRs 0027 to 0031)**: this ADR is 0032. I did not add it to the `adr/README.org` table, because #419 edits the same rows; add the row after #419 merges.\n- #435, #434: not touched.\n\n## Why\n\n- Sia: the printed-to-physical page information should live in the PDF itself, not in Emacs or the record. Page labels (`/PageLabels`) are the PDF's own way to say \"physical page 1 is 360\".\n- Decision and alternatives: `adr/0032-page-labels-live-in-the-pdf.org`. Nothing is implemented inside DEVONthink (no metadata, no AppleScript).\n\n## Change\n\n- Literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/pdf-page-labels.org` tangles to `tools/pdf_page_labels.py` (library), three tools and `tests/test_pdf_page_labels.py`.\n- `tools/pdf-labels-articles.py` (batch): dry run unless `--apply`.\n  - Handles `article`, `inproceedings`, `conference`, `suppperiodical` with no `crossref`/`xref` (`--types` widens it); skips and reports `book`, `collection`, `incollection`, `inbook`, theses, reports and the rest.\n  - First page of `pages`: `360--364`, `360-364`, `e123` (label `e123`), `xii--xv` (roman), upper-case roman; anything else is skipped with the reason.\n  - Skips a PDF that already has different labels unless `--force`; reports unchanged ones; warns when the page range length differs from the PDF's page count.\n  - Options: `--only KEY`, `--bib`, `--bib-dir`, `--library`, `--backup-dir`, `--verbose`.\n- `tools/pdf-labels-book.py CITEKEY-OR-PDF --first-page N [--front-roman ...]`: one book, never reads `pages`; dry run unless `--apply`.\n- Writing is safe: save to a temp file, re-open and check page count and labels, copy the original to `~/.local/state/pdf-page-labels/backups/TIMESTAMP/...`, then replace.\n- `tools/pdf-labels-read.py FILE --resolve LABEL`: the reader Emacs calls (exit 3 no labels, 4 not found).\n- `sp-devonthink`: `sp-devonthink-first-page-label`, `sp-devonthink-pdf-page-for-label`, options `sp-devonthink-label-command` and `sp-devonthink-label-script`; the two offset options are removed. With no labels or no match, the parent opens at the start with a message saying why.\n- Needs `pikepdf` (`pip install pikepdf`); each tool also has a `uv run` inline dependency. qpdf alone is not enough for lookup.\n- No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## What was verified and what was not\n\n- [x] 29 Python tests (`python3 -m unittest tests/test_pdf_page_labels.py`) on generated PDFs: parsing, BibTeX reader, round trip, backup, failed save leaves the original, both tools in dry run and `--apply`, the reader's exit codes.\n- [x] 28 ERT tests pass (one runs the real reader script on a generated PDF); tangle check passes.\n- **DEVONthink page counting (from documentation, not run):**\n  - [DEVONtechnologies forum](https://discourse.devontechnologies.com/t/x-devonthink-item-link-from-pdf-expert-with-page-number/55617): a staff reply says the `page` parameter of an item link is zero-based.\n  - [DEVONthink blog](https://www.devontechnologies.com/blog/20220208-pdf-page-numbering): copied page links point at the page number, not the folio; `?page=12` opens physical page 13.\n  - This matches the existing code (`?page=N-1`) and the `sp-litdb` measurement.\n- **Not checked:**\n  - whether DEVONthink shows or uses the PDF's page labels in its own page display or links (the docs I found don't say; the code assumes links stay physical);\n  - the base of `current page` in AppleScript (still `sp-devonthink-store-page-offset`);\n  - `pikepdf` on the Mac, `python3` there being one that has it, and any real PDF of yours (everything ran on generated PDFs on Linux);\n  - the `file` field forms in your real `.bib` files beyond relative paths, `JabRef` triples and name lookup; entries that only have `bdsk-file-N` are not found.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `pip install pikepdf` (or note the `uv run` route), then `tools/pdf-labels-articles.py --only KEY` for one journal article: a dry run lists `would-label KEY ... first page 360` and writes nothing.\n- [ ] Same with `--apply --only KEY`: the PDF opens in Preview or DEVONthink with pages 360 to 364 shown; a copy of the original is under `~/.local/state/pdf-page-labels/backups/`.\n- [ ] Run it again: reported `unchanged`.\n- [ ] `tools/pdf-labels-articles.py` for the whole library, dry run: read the skip reasons (no PDF, unparseable pages, several PDFs); check the warnings about page ranges that differ from the PDF length.\n- [ ] Entry with `pages = {e123}` and one with `xii--xv`: labels `e123, e124, ...` and `xii, xiii, ...`.\n- [ ] A `book` and an `incollection` entry are not touched.\n- [ ] Book whose printed page 1 is the 9th PDF page: `tools/pdf-labels-book.py KEY --first-page 9 --front-roman` (dry run), then `--apply`; the viewer shows i to viii and then 1.\n- [ ] A chapter of that book in citar, `embark-act` then `D`: DEVONthink opens the book at the chapter's first page; the echo area says `from the PDF's page labels`.\n- [ ] If it opens one page off, say which way: DEVONthink may be counting differently than the docs say.\n- [ ] A chapter whose parent PDF has no labels: opens at the start; the message says to run `pdf-labels-book.py`.\n- [ ] If the message says it could not read the labels, check `(setq sp-devonthink-label-command '(\"uv\" \"run\" \"--script\"))` or a Python that has `pikepdf`.\n- [ ] Check that DEVONthink still finds and opens a PDF after it was labelled (the file's bytes changed).\n\n## Revert guide\n\n- Restore a PDF: copy the file from `~/.local/state/pdf-page-labels/backups/TIMESTAMP/<original path>` over it. To remove the labels instead, run `tools/pdf-labels-book.py KEY --first-page 1 --apply`, which writes plain `1, 2, 3, ...`.\n- Revert the code: `git revert` the single commit of this PR. That restores the offset options and `sp-devonthink-first-page` from #436; the tools and the ADR go away. PDFs already labelled keep their labels, which are harmless to other programs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBXqXW4Xbxy8r2aJtW)_",
